Skyward — third-party content
=============================

Skyward's own code is GPL-2.0-or-later (see LICENSE). It bundles content by
others; per-item sources, authors and licences are listed in:

  * assets/aircraft/<id>/CREDITS.md — aircraft models, textures and JSBSim
    flight-dynamics data converted from FlightGear aircraft (GPL v2 / v2+;
    the A320-family is GPL v2 only). The v3 heavies are GPL v2 (the
    packages ship the GPL v2 text with no "or later" clause):
      - hercules: FGAddon trunk/Aircraft/C130 (SVN r21799), GPL-2.0
        (Emmanuel Baranger, Didier Fabert, Jettoo);
      - galaxy: github.com/FGMEMBERS/C-5 (33ec1e31), GPL-2.0
        (Jon Bourgeois, Gary Scott, Peter Brendt);
      - vulcan: github.com/FGMEMBERS/AvroVulcanB2 (FGUK, 3064c65f), GPL-2.0
        (Stuart Buchanan, FGUK; after Jonathan Harris's GPL X-Plane model),
        including its engine recordings (assets/audio/samples/vul_*).
    The H2a jets:
      - triple7: FGAddon trunk/Aircraft/777 (SVN r21799), GPL-2.0
        (Syd Adams, Justin Smithies, Thorsten Brehm, Joshua Davidson,
        Isaak Dieleman et al.); the package's plain white livery;
      - crj700: github.com/FGMEMBERS/CRJ700-family (4862db2f, 2016:
        "models, textures, markup and scripts" GPL-2.0-or-later — later
        FGAddon revisions moved the models / textures to CC-BY-4.0 and are
        not used) and the FGAddon CRJ700jsb JSBSim FDM (SVN r21799,
        markup GPL-2.0-or-later) (Ryan Miller, Daniel Meissner et al.);
      - citationx: github.com/FGMEMBERS/CitationX (e497ad98), GPL-2.0
        (repository COPYING; Syd Adams et al.);
      - concorde: FGAddon trunk/Aircraft/Concorde (SVN r21799; FDM header
        "GPL", FGMEMBERS mirror COPYING GPL-2.0) (FlightGear Concorde
        developers); livery repainted plain white (no airline marks).
    The rotorcraft (Track Q):
      - ec130: FGAddon trunk/Aircraft/ec130 (SVN r21799), GPL-2.0-or-later
        (Heiko Schulz, Melchior Franz, Michael Habarta); neutral livery
        derived from the package's default texture;
      - fpv: the FPV quadcopter's model is Skyward's own, built in code
        (src/rotor/quad_model.rs), no third-party content.
    Track H2b (more propeller types), FGAddon trunk SVN r21799:
      - extra500: FGAddon extra500, GPL-2.0-or-later (Dirk Dittmann,
        Eric van den Berg, Thomas Grossberger);
      - cub: FGAddon Piper-PA-18, GPL-2.0 (Emmanuel Baranger);
      - zlin: FGAddon Zlin-50lx, GPL-2.0 (Emmanuel Baranger, Pierre
        Geoffroy, Sebastien Marque, Laurent Hayvel);
      - otter: FGAddon dhc3, GPL-2.0 (Emmanuel Baranger, Pierre Geoffroy);
      - dc3: FGAddon Douglas-Dc3, GPL-2.0 (Emmanuel Baranger, Gary Neely,
        the PAF team), including its engine recordings
        (assets/audio/samples/r18_*); neutral livery derived from the
        package's default texture.
  * assets/audio/CREDITS.md — sounds, including FlightGear recordings
    (GPL v2 / v2+, some GPL v2 only).
  * assets/audio/atc/ — ATC / ATIS radio voice clips generated for Skyward
    with Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0 model; the clips are original output,
    released with the project — see assets/audio/CREDITS.md).
  * assets/fonts/ — fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1).
  * README.md, "Credits" — map, weather and airport data services. Navaids
    (VOR, DME, NDB) come from OurAirports' navaids.csv (public domain,
    https://ourairports.com/data/); ILS localizer / glideslope records are
    synthetic, derived from the OurAirports runway data (src/nav/db.rs), with
    the frequencies, idents and glidepath angles of a few London ILS taken as
    facts from public charts. Airport radio frequencies (ATIS, delivery,
    ground, tower, approach) come from OurAirports' airport-frequencies.csv
    (public domain). No licence-restricted navigation data is used.
  * Live traffic (src/adsb/): aircraft positions from the adsb.lol API,
    made available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0
    (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/) — © adsb.lol
    contributors. tests/adsb/*.json are anonymised extracts of it (synthetic
    addresses, no registrations, re-numbered flights), under the same licence.

Because some bundled content is GPL version 2 only, the combined work is
distributed under the terms of GPL version 2.
